_site
.sass-cache
.jekyll-cache
.jekyll-metadata
vendor

# CV source PDFs — these carry personal contact details and, more importantly,
# referees' direct emails and mobile numbers. This repo is public, so keeping
# them untracked matters even though _config.yml also excludes them from the
# built site: committing them would expose the files on github.com regardless
# of whether Jekyll publishes them.
CV_*.pdf

# Concatenated full text of published papers, kept locally as a reference for
# maintaining _data/publications.yml. Includes publisher-typeset versions
# (e.g. the Elsevier Hexpo article) that should not be redistributed.
All_Publications.md

# Raw research data must never enter this repo — it is public.
#
# The working datasets live in ../Data and belong there. Two of them are
# individual-level personal health data:
#   * Covid_Data.csv — a patient line list with LAB IDs, symptoms, COVID/TB/
#     pneumococcal results, region and district. Pseudonymous, not anonymous.
#   * "Behavioral insights for COVID-19 in Ghana (Responses).xlsx" — a
#     214-column survey export whose respondents consented to a specific
#     WHO/GHS/UHAS study, not to open publication.
#
# Posts should carry aggregates and charts, never the underlying records. These
# patterns are a backstop in case a file is ever copied in here by accident.
*.xlsx
*.xls
Covid_Data.csv
BOGnew.csv
/Data/
/data/
